Notebook[{
Cell["Caldeira-Leggett High-T Lindblad: Symbolic Exploration", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Working document. It develops the symbolic (closed-form) track of ",
 Cell["exploration-plan.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 ": given the paper's main outcome, the master equation of arXiv:2508.14262, \
which of its features can be extracted in closed form that are physically \
important and carry useful impact. Each feature below is stated with why it \
matters, then explored; every symbolic result was reproduced in a kernel. \
Companions: ",
 Cell["caldeira-leggett-high-T-lindblad.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " (Layers 0-1 essay), ",
 Cell["related-papers/tex/2508.14262/", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " (paper source)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["The generator, and what \"symbolic\" means here", "Section",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
The object of study is the general three-coefficient Dekker generator, the \
most general Markovian quantum-Brownian-motion master equation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ". Its quadratic structure is inherited from the model (a particle coupled \
bilinearly to a harmonic bath); reducing to a Markovian, constant-coefficient \
generator at all is the Born-Markov assumption, the exact dynamics being \
non-Markovian (Hu-Paz-Zhang for a harmonic potential). The paper's result is \
one distinguished point in this family,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"6", 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
     SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "pinned by four assumptions: an Ohmic bath, weak coupling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[LessLess]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ", the cutoff removed at fixed temperature (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LessLess]", "\[HBar]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 "), and keeping only the leading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 " correction past white noise. The first three make the coefficients \
cutoff-free and give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 "; relax one and they move, a different bath rescales them, the other scale \
ordering gives Di\[OAcute]si or Breuer-Petruccione with a cutoff-dependent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 ", and higher order adds lower-temperature corrections. Everything symbolic \
below explores this one point."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every term is at most quadratic in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " except the Hamiltonian commutator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", "\[CenterDot]"}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 ": for quadratic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " the dynamics closes on the first two moments and everything is closed \
form, while for anharmonic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " the hierarchy opens and simulation takes over. The high-impact symbolic \
features live in the quadratic (harmonic and free) case, plus one basis-level \
fact that holds for any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell["The features worth exploring, and why", "Section",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell["\<\
Two questions must be kept apart: which features close in symbolic form (many \
do), and which are genuinely new (few are). Take the audit first, then the \
results that clear the bar.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["The four features below reproduce or reframe. By \
themselves they do not add to the literature.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A. Thermalization pins ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 StyleBox[".",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "6", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " off the equilibrium momentum variance, with complete positivity following, \
is a clean ",
 StyleBox["reframing", "TI"],
 " of the paper's positivity argument, and the sharpest of the four. It is \
not new physics. That a completely positive Markovian generator cannot sit \
exactly at the Gibbs state, and that the position-diffusion term restoring \
positivity is precisely what sustains a steady phase-space current with \
nonzero entropy production, was established for the general Dekker family by \
Artini, Lo Monaco, Imparato, Paternostro and Donadi (arXiv:2507.23322); the \
inverse route, fixing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["from", "TI"],
 " the entropy production, is Bern\[AAcute]d, Homa and Csirik (Eur. Phys. J. \
D ",
 StyleBox["72",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 212 (2018)). Feature A is their statement, specialized to the paper's \
point, and section A below adds the exact version of the tension."
}], "Item",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["B. Decoherence and classicalization.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Quantifies the paper's own title claim by reading the two \
double-commutator rates off the generator. Reproduction."
}], "Item",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["C. The Wigner picture.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The textbook Wigner transform of the generator into a Klein-Kramers \
equation. Reproduction."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Engine. The moment hierarchy.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The standard Ehrenfest-plus-diffusion moment ladder from the adjoint \
generator. Reproduction."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell["\<\
So of the four, only A carries a useful idea, and even that idea's deep half, \
the thermalization-positivity tension, is already known.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The bar, and where the frontier actually is.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A referee credits what neither the paper nor the literature already holds. \
Two directions looked promising, and testing them was the point: the \
systematic low-temperature extension of the kernel, and a sharp \
thermalization error against Gibbs. Both turn out to be settled, and settled \
correctly, in places this document must defer to rather than duplicate. \
Reporting that plainly is the honest result here."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The systematic expansion is done, and it converges.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The companion essay carries the fluctuation-path expansion to all orders (",
 Cell["caldeira-leggett-high-T-lindblad.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 ", Parts VI-VII). The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 " coefficients are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 "; the even-derivative tower resums to the exact Ohmic spectrum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\\", "coth"}], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 "; complete positivity is special to the two-term order, since the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " channel variance is negative (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "4"], "<", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 "); the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " operator is the free acceleration ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 ", so it stays in the harmonic (X,X) channel and becomes a new Lindblad \
operator only for anharmonic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 "; and each order deepens the Gibbs match by one power of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ", the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " term cancelling the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " miss exactly. Decisively, the series is ",
 StyleBox["convergent", "TI"],
 ", radius set by the first Matsubara frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ". The raw moments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " do grow factorially, but the smooth-path reduction supplies a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " that turns them into the decaying coefficients above, so the tower \
converges down to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Tilde]", "\[HBar]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 ". Any \"asymptotic, keep-one-term-is-optimal\" reading of this hierarchy is \
wrong: the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " is the whole point, and it lives in the coefficient, not the bare moment."
}], "Item",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The equilibrium error is a known kind.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " That a completely positive Markovian steady state departs from Gibbs \
beyond leading order in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " is established (arXiv:2305.06312), and the broken-detailed-balance side, \
the steady correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " and its entropy production, is Artini, Lo Monaco, Imparato, Paternostro \
and Donadi (arXiv:2507.23322) and Bern\[AAcute]d, Homa and Csirik (Eur. Phys. \
J. D ",
 StyleBox["72",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 212 (2018)). Section A below makes the \
completely-positive-versus-thermalization tension exact for this family, but \
as an illustration of that known result, not a new one."
}], "Item",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell["\<\
So neither promising direction is new. The genuinely open frontier, settled \
by neither the essay nor the broken-detailed-balance literature, was two \
questions. The first is now answered, in closed form, in its own section \
below.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mean force, not bare Gibbs: answered.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A weakly coupled open system equilibrates not to the bare Gibbs state but \
to the mean-force Gibbs state, whose reduced covariance differs at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ". Are the completely positive steady state's deviations from bare Gibbs \
those mean-force corrections in disguise? The section \"Mean force, not bare \
Gibbs\" below answers no in two lines (the generator's diagonal has no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " deviation at all; its steady correlation sits against a time-reversal \
zero), then computes what holding the mean-force covariance would take. On \
the Caldeira-Leggett friction slice, exact stationarity of any diagonal \
covariance costs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " (the Dekker-Valsakumar floor; the slice impossibility is in Isar's \
thermal-generator formulas), no matter how the Hamiltonian is renormalized; \
the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 " mean-force corrections are cutoff-dependent in momentum and odd in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " in position, the latter structurally beyond the local kernel expansion's \
even, diagonal sources (the parity scoping is the one genuinely unasked \
question here); and the slice-versus-wider-family dichotomy is Artini and \
co-workers' translation-covariance theorem, rendered as a single closed-form \
slack whose completely positive equilibrating window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 " shows the obstruction to be exactly critical. The exact Hu-Paz-Zhang \
dynamics shares the slice signature (no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " term, a time-dependent cross coefficient, mean-force endpoint), which \
yields one falsifiable prediction, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["det",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"H", "P", "Z"}], "TI"], 
     RowBox[{" ", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]}]]}], "\[LessEqual]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Infinity]", "2"]}], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 ", posed conventions-pinned in Next steps."
}], "Item",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Hu-Paz-Zhang benchmark, quantitatively.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Both the two-term generator and the exact non-Markovian dynamics are \
Gaussian for harmonic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 ", so their covariance difference along the transient is a closed-form \
contest between truncation error and memory. The equilibrium endpoints are \
settled by the mean-force section below (the exact late-time state is the \
mean-force Gibbs state); what remains open is the transient, which the essay \
sets up (Part VIII)."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sections A and B carry the established closed-form results, and section A \
makes the equilibrium tension exact. The mean-force section is the new work. \
The Wigner picture (C) and the moment hierarchy (Engine) remain the \
general-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " tools, set up at the end."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A. Thermalization pins ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 "; positivity is a corollary"
}], "Section",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the harmonic case ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 ", where the steady state is Gaussian and exact. The physical question is \
whether the master equation relaxes to the quantum canonical (Gibbs) state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "/", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 ", whose covariance is known in closed form (the positivity assumptions are \
declared once here and every algebraic step below inherits them):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Om", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"aa", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"bb", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"lam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Ms", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ws", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sXXgibbs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "M", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
      RowBox[{"w0", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sPPgibbs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "M", " ", 
    RowBox[{"w0", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
      RowBox[{"w0", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sPPgibbs", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The high-temperature expansion of the Gibbs momentum variance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"12", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 ": the classical equipartition value plus the leading quantum thermal \
correction of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the master equation's steady covariance. The Lyapunov equation solves \
in one stroke for the ",
 StyleBox["full", "TI"],
 " three-coefficient family, the diffusion matrix carrying the Dekker \
coefficients as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", "2", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "{", "{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "}", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Amat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "M"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "M"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"diffusion", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dxx_", ",", " ", "dpp_", ",", " ", "dxp_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "dxp"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "dxp"}], ",", " ", "dpp"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sigmaGen", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Amat", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"diffusion", "[", 
         RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
     ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "Reals"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", "sigmaGen"}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The general steady covariance of the family in closed form, and its \
structure is already the physics: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " depends on the position-diffusion coefficient alone, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " sees only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ", and the cross coefficient enters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 " only. It is the genuine stationary solution, residual identically zero:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Amat", " ", ".", " ", "sigmaGen"}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"sigmaGen", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "Amat", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"diffusion", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell["\<\
And the steady state exists and is unique because the drift is Hurwitz:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "Amat", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The damped-oscillator poles ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 "; that both stay in the open left half-plane for all positive parameters is \
one quantifier elimination via the Routh-Hurwitz form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Resolve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ForAll", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"M", ",", " ", "w0", ",", " ", "gam"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "Amat", "]"}], " ", "<", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Det", "[", "Amat", "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", "Reals"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Relaxation happens on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " timescale, independent of temperature and of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 ". Now specialize to the paper's channel structure, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " at the Einstein value and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", keeping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " free so we can see what value the physics wants:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steady", "[", "d_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"steady", "[", "d", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{"sigmaGen", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dxx", " ", "->", " ", "d"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dpp", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
          RowBox[{"T", "/", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dxp", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"steady", "[", "dxx", "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The steady momentum variance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ", linear in the new coefficient. Setting it equal to the Gibbs value fixes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"steady", "[", "dxx", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
      RowBox[{"sPPgibbs", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",",
    " ", "dxx"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The unique solution is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 ", exactly the paper's coefficient. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 " is not a free positivity-restoring parameter: it is the value, and the \
only value, that makes the equilibrium momentum fluctuation \
quantum-mechanically correct to order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Complete positivity is then automatic, and it is worth building the \
Kossakowski matrix as an object rather than quoting its determinant from \
memory. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " the determinant is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "4", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], "-", "4", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"], "2"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 ", and its zero over the whole family:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dxx_", ",", " ", "dpp_", ",", " ", "dxp_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "dpp"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxp"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxx"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
     RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
        RowBox[{"T", "/", 
         RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ",
     "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", "dxx"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The positivity floor is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "+", "4", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"], "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "8", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 ", minimized at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " where it reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "8", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ": cross diffusion only raises it, so every bound derived below at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 " holds a fortiori across the family. Two facts make this matrix trustworthy \
rather than quoted. First, it is faithful to the generator: the GKSL \
dissipator built from it with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " equals the Dekker double-commutator form once a frequency-renormalization \
Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "{", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 " is split off into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"e", "f", "f"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " (the Lamb shift the paper's footnote absorbs), an operator identity on a \
truncated Fock carrier with everything symbolic:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"nn", " ", "=", " ", "6"}], ",", " ", "a", ",", " ", "x", ",", 
     " ", "p", ",", " ", "comm", ",", " ", "acomm", ",", " ", "rho", ",", " ",
      "aK", ",", " ", "ls", ",", " ", "gksl", ",", " ", "dekker", ",", " ", 
     "lamb"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"nn", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "M", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"I", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "M", " ", 
        RowBox[{"w0", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "a"}], ")"}]}]}],
     ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"u_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"u", " ", ".", " ", "v"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", "u"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"u_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"u", " ", ".", " ", "v"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", "u"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ls", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"aK", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"gksl", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"aK", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ls", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}],
          ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"dekker", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dpp", " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", 
      "     ", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "dxp", " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"lamb", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"acomm", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Union", " ", "@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Flatten", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Simplify", " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"gksl", " ", "-", " ", "dekker", " ", "-", " ", "lamb"}], 
          ")"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
        "]"}]}]}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The interior block vanishes for arbitrary symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["M", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 ", coefficients, and state, so the Kossakowski matrix is the generator, up \
to a Hamiltonian shift that touches no positivity statement. Second, the \
determinant is the binding constraint but not the whole criterion; positive \
semidefiniteness needs the diagonal too, and at the paper's point the full \
spectrum clears:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Resolve", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ForAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "hbar", ",", " ", "M", ",", " ", "gam", ",", " ", "kB", ",", " ", "T"}], 
     "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
        RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", 
           RowBox[{"T", "/", 
            RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
       " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both eigenvalues are nonnegative at every temperature, mass, and coupling. \
The three coefficients line up as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", " ", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"6", 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"thermal", ",", "\[ThinSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"this", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "work"}]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"8", 
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], " ", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"minimal", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "positivity"}], ",", 
        "\[ThinSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
        RowBox[{"Breuer", "-", "Petruccione"}]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"Caldeira", "-", "Leggett"}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], " ", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 ". The thermal value exceeds the positivity threshold by a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "/", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 ", so getting the equilibrium fluctuation right guarantees a completely \
positive generator with margin to spare. Breuer-Petruccione sits exactly on \
the positivity boundary but undershoots the thermal correction (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "/", "16", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " against the correct ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "/", "12", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 "); Caldeira-Leggett has neither."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How closely the full covariance matches Gibbs, term by term in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
        
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       "sPPgibbs"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
        
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       "sXXgibbs"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The momentum variance matches the Gibbs state through order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 ", its first surviving difference the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 "-free ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 " term now visible. The position variance matches to order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " with a residual ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 ", and there is a steady position-momentum correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 " that the Gibbs state does not have. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 " residuals are simultaneously quantum and dissipative, vanishing in the \
weak-coupling limit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 ", exactly the regime where a Markovian generator is meant to hold; the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " pieces are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 "-free truncation residues that survive even that limit. Standard \
Caldeira-Leggett, by contrast, misses the quantum correction entirely: its \
steady state is the classical equipartition covariance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 ", off from Gibbs by order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 " in both entries."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Whatever its distance from Gibbs, the steady state is a legal quantum \
state, and not just at the paper's point: for ",
 StyleBox["every", "TI"],
 " completely positive member of the family the \
Robertson-Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger bound holds, provable outright as one \
quantifier elimination over the coefficients themselves:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Resolve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ForAll", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "hbar", ",", " ", "M", ",", " ", "w0", ",", " ", "gam", ",", " ", "dxx",
        ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dpp", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "dxx", " ", "dpp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dxp", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gam", "^", "2"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}], " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Det", "[", "sigmaGen", "]"}], " ", ">=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell["\<\
Complete positivity of the generator implies the uncertainty floor for its \
steady covariance, at every temperature, mass, frequency, coupling, and \
admissible coefficient triple: the advertised job, done at the Gaussian \
level, family-wide.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell["\<\
The section's closed forms deserve one reference computed by an entirely \
different route: the full density-matrix Liouvillian on a truncated Fock \
space, evolved to stationarity, against the Lyapunov closed form at the same \
point:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"nn", " ", "=", " ", "40"}], ",", " ", "a", ",", " ", "x", ",", 
     " ", "p", ",", " ", "id", ",", " ", "kp", ",", " ", "h", ",", " ", 
     "lmat", ",", " ", "v0", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "rho", ",", " ", "tr", ",",
      " ", "mom", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamN", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"N", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
           RowBox[{"nn", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2.", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"I", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "a"}], ")"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2.", "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"id", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"N", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "SparseArray"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"kp", " ", "=", " ", "KroneckerProduct"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"h", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "x"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"lmat", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"h", ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "h", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "gamN", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], " ", "+",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "p", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "x", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ",
       "-", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "gamN", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "x"}], ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], " ", "-",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "x", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ",
       "-", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gamN", "/", "6"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], " ", "-",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
           RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "p", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], 
    ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"v0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Flatten", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1.", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"0.", " ", "I"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    
    RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"lmat", " ", "120."}], ",", " ", "v0"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
      RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "nn"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"tr", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"mom", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Re", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "x", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}], ",",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], " ", "+", " ", 
               RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "x"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
             "rho"}], "]"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
           RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "p", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], 
         "}"}], "/", "tr"}], ")"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"mom", ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"N", " ", "@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
        " ", "&"}], "[", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"steady", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gam", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"M", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"w0", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gam", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"kB", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"T", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"tr", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Max", " ", "@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{"rho", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "rho", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Min", " ", "@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", " ", "@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"rho", " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "tr"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        
        RowBox[{"Total", " ", "@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Abs", " ", "@", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", "rho", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "4"}], " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell["\<\
The first two rows agree: the density operator relaxed from the ground state \
under the full generator reaches the covariance the Lyapunov algebra \
predicts, an end-to-end check that touches the operators, not the moment \
equations. The third row holds the run's own legality certificates, trace \
drift, Hermiticity defect, smallest eigenvalue, and the population of the top \
truncation levels; all sit at numerical noise, so the evolution neither \
leaked probability nor left the physical state space, and the agreement above \
is not laundered by the normalization.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why this matters.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The paper motivates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " by positivity. The symbolic reading is cleaner: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " is fixed by thermalization, it is the coefficient that recovers the \
leading quantum correction to the equilibrium state, and positivity follows \
because that thermal value happens to exceed the positivity threshold. The \
new term repairs the equilibrium, not merely the spectrum of the generator, \
and it upgrades the master equation from correct-to-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 " to correct-to-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " at fixed temperature."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The tension, made exact.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The match to Gibbs is only to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 ", and it must be. Ask instead for the generator whose steady state is ",
 StyleBox["exactly", "TI"],
 " the Gibbs covariance, at all orders in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 ". The Lyapunov equation inverts, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"G", "i", "b", "b", "s"}], "TI"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"G", "i", "b", "b", "s"}], "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[UpTee]"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ", and returns a unique diffusion matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"lyapInv", "[", 
    RowBox[{"a_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", " ", ".", " ", "s"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "a", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sigGibbs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"sXXgibbs", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "sPPgibbs"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Dreq", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"lyapInv", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Amat", ",", " ", "sigGibbs"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Dreq", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact-thermalizing diffusion is diagonal with a vanishing position \
slot. Read its Dekker coefficients back through the same ",
 Cell[BoxData["diffusion"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " map:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"diffusion", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
     " ", "Dreq"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The generator that thermalizes exactly has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 ": it is the position-coupling-only generator carrying the full \
Bose-Einstein momentum diffusion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "\[HBar]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\\", "coth"}], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 ", the quantum-corrected Caldeira-Leggett equation. Its Kossakowski \
determinant is negative at every temperature:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "M", " ", "w0", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
         RowBox[{"w0", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], "/", 
       "hbar"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the exact-thermalizing generator is not completely positive: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "<", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 ", the diffusion-constraint floor of Dekker and Valsakumar (Phys. Lett. A ",
 StyleBox["104",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 67 (1984)). Complete positivity needs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "8", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 ", and any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " pushes the steady correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " off its equilibrium value of zero, opening the phase-space current. Exact \
thermalization and complete positivity are therefore mutually exclusive ",
 StyleBox["on the Caldeira-Leggett friction slice and for a confining \
potential", "TI"],
 " (for a free particle the momentum marginal is exactly Maxwellian, though \
the steady correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 " survives even there); the wider two-parameter friction family escapes (the \
quantum-optical damped oscillator is completely positive with an exact Gibbs \
steady state, see the mean-force section). Both halves of that dichotomy are \
the theorem of Artini and co-workers on translation-covariant completely \
positive quadratic master equations, with the entropy production as its \
thermodynamic reading. The paper's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "6", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 " and Breuer-Petruccione's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "8", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " are then two named compromises inside the completely positive cone: the \
former is the point that gets the equilibrium ",
 StyleBox["energy", "TI"],
 " right (the momentum variance exact to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 "), the latter the ",
 StyleBox["minimal", "TI"],
 " completely positive point (the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " boundary), their ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "/", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 " being the paper's positivity margin."
}], "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell["B. Decoherence and classicalization, quantified", "Section",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two double commutators are diagonal in position and in momentum \
respectively, so their decohering action is read off directly. The \
load-bearing identity, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]},
      "Bra"], 
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]},
     "Bra"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 ", is one cell on a position grid:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"xs", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xg", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", "xs", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
         RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "x", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], " ", "-", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "x"}]}], " ", "+", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "x", " ", ".", " ", "x"}]}], " ", "==", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Subtract", ",", " ", "xs", ",", " ", "xs"}], "]"}], "^", 
         "2"}], " ", "rho"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The double commutator multiplies each matrix element by the squared \
separation of its grid points, and by Fourier symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 " does the same in momentum with weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 ". Hence an off-diagonal element decays exponentially at a rate quadratic in \
the separation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "position superposition of separation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 ";"
}], "Item",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "momentum superposition of separation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"6", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second rate is the new channel and is exactly the paper's \"penalizing \
high-frequency fluctuations\": a superposition that is broad in momentum \
(fine, high-spatial-frequency interference structure) is damped in proportion \
to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 ". The two rates carry opposite temperature dependence, seen in their ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 "-derivatives:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"D", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dx", "^", "2"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "T"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"D", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dp", "^", "2"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"6", " ", "M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     "T"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell["\<\
Position decoherence strengthens with temperature (the familiar \
thermal-wavelength suppression of spatial coherence), while momentum \
decoherence weakens with temperature. Their ratio,\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"12", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "says the new channel dominates for momentum-broad superpositions and at \
lower temperature. This is a concrete, testable fingerprint of the corrected \
generator that the standard Caldeira-Leggett equation (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 ") does not produce at all: it decoheres position but never momentum."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell["\<\
Mean force, not bare Gibbs: where the equilibrium statement ends\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The frontier question above has a short answer and a longer lesson. The \
comparison target is exactly known: the late-time state of the \
Caldeira-Leggett model is the ",
 StyleBox["mean-force Gibbs state", "TI"],
 ", the reduced state of the global Gibbs state of system plus bath (Suba\
\:015f\[DotlessI], Fleming, Taylor and Hu, Phys. Rev. E ",
 StyleBox["86",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 061132 (2012)); for the Ohmic damped oscillator its covariance is a \
Matsubara sum with a closed form (Grabert, Schramm and Ingold, Phys. Rep. ",
 StyleBox["168",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 115 (1988); the modern mean-force program is Cresser and Anders, Phys. \
Rev. Lett. ",
 StyleBox["127",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 250601 (2021) and the review of Trushechkin, Merkli, Cresser and Anders, \
AVS Quantum Sci. ",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 012301 (2022)). At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " the mean-force state is the bare Gibbs state, so feature A's target was \
correct at its order; the two part ways at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ". The short answer is then already on the page: by feature A, the \
generator's diagonal deviations from bare Gibbs are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " with no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " term at all, while the mean-force corrections computed below are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 "; and its steady correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "6", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 " sits against an exact zero. The deviations are not mean-force corrections \
in disguise; nothing was hiding. The longer lesson is what holding the \
mean-force covariance stationary would actually take, with the \
Caldeira-Leggett friction structure and with the bare Hamiltonian, and what \
each of those two qualifiers is worth. That requires the mean-force \
corrections in closed form first."
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact equilibrium position variance is the Matsubara sum over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " with the damping entering through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 ", in closed form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", "n", " ", "kB", " ", 
    RowBox[{"T", "/", "hbar"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"sxxMF", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"kB", " ", 
      RowBox[{"T", "/", "M"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", "/", 
       RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", 
             RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], 
        "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "//", "\n", "   ", 
   "FullSimplify"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A digamma pair at the two relaxation frequencies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],
 " of the damped oscillator (the Euler constants of the two harmonic numbers \
cancel in the difference), one expression for both branches: overdamped the \
arguments are real, underdamped they are complex conjugates and the imaginary \
parts cancel. Three independent routes must give one number: this closed \
form, the raw Matsubara sum, and the fluctuation-dissipation integral ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]",
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   RowBox[{"\\", "coth"}], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["Im",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 ". At one benign underdamped point:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"M", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kB", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"7", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "g"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"N", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Chop", " ", "@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"N", "[", 
           RowBox[{"sxxMF", ",", " ", "20"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"kB", " ", 
           RowBox[{"T", "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"M", " ", 
              RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", 
           RowBox[{"T", "/", "M"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"NSum", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"1", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
             "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"NSumTerms", " ", "->", " ", "200"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", " ", "->", " ", "30"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
         ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"NIntegrate", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", "/", "Pi"}], ")"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
              RowBox[{"w", "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"Im", "[", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"M", " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"2", " ", "I", " ", "gam", " ", "w"}]}], ")"}]}], 
               ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", " ", "->", " ", "20"}]}], "]"}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", "12"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"3", "/", "10"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"5", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One number three ways in each row, the first row underdamped and the second \
overdamped, so both branches of the closed form are exercised; a convention \
slip in any route, a factor of two in the friction, a misplaced ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " in the Matsubara frequency, would break the agreement loudly. Two sanity \
limits pin the closed form to known physics. The uncoupled limit must return \
the Gibbs variance:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
     RowBox[{"sxxMF", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gam", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", 
    " ", "sXXgibbs"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The difference vanishes: at zeroth order in the coupling, mean force and \
bare Gibbs coincide. And the classical limit must lose the coupling entirely, \
at every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
    RowBox[{"sxxMF", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Classical equipartition, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 "-free: for the harmonic Caldeira-Leggett model with its counterterm, the \
classical mean-force correction is identically zero, so every mean-force \
correction below is a quantum effect. The one place the closed form \
degenerates is critical damping, where the two relaxation frequencies collide \
and the square root vanishes; the limit closes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{"sxxMF", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gam", " ", "->", " ", "w0"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"w0", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finite, a single trigamma at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "+", "\[HBar]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 ": the degeneracy is removable. The free-particle boundary is not, and on \
the generator's side all three entries of the story sit in one limit of the \
covariance already computed:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"steady", "[", "dxx", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"steady", "[", "dxx", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"steady", "[", "dxx", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"w0", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"hbar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"M", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kB", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The momentum marginal is exactly Maxwellian (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],
 ", no ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 " at any order), the steady correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 " survives untouched, and the position variance has no stationary value at \
all; this is the computation behind the free-particle statements in section A \
and below. Now the object of interest, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 " coefficient of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"M", "F"}], "TI"]], "-", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"G", "i", "b", "b", "s"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"c1", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", 
      RowBox[{"T", "/", "M"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", 
              RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "gam"}], 
         "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gam", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A trigamma pair at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", "\[Pi]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],
 ". Its high-temperature expansion exposes the structure that matters:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{"c1", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"hbar", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "7"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The series through order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "7"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 " has only odd terms, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "5"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "7"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 ", with no even power anywhere. The leading coefficient is a zeta value:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PolyGamma", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Zeta", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the true equilibrium position variance carries the correction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "3", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "3"], "/", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "3"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " at leading order: finite, cutoff-free, negative, and ",
 StyleBox["odd in ", "TI"],
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula", "TI",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 " at every order shown. Neither the number nor the physics is a discovery. \
The coefficient is the next term of the standard large-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],
 " expansion of the Grabert-Schramm-Ingold Matsubara sum, the first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 "-dependent one (the preceding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "2", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 " term is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 "-free Wigner-Kirkwood correction, where Hilt, Thomas and Lutz stop, Phys. \
Rev. E ",
 StyleBox["84",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 031110 (2011), whose reading of the sign, the bath as a continuous \
position measurement squeezing the variance, carries over). What matters for \
this section is not the constant but the parity: the correction is odd in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 ". Against it the generator offers nothing to compare: at the paper's point \
the steady ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],
 " is even in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],
 ", so its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 " mean-force correction is not badly approximated, it is absent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Odd is one obstruction, with a sharp scope. On the Markovian side, the \
Lyapunov diffusion source contributed by the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],
 "-th term of the local kernel expansion (the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],
 " tower of the essay) is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],
 " times the coefficient over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 "-free channel factors; that weight-to-coefficient map is quoted from the \
essay's Part IV, and given it, the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 "-content is even at every order:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"c2n", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], "^", "n"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BernoulliB", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}], "!"}]}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Exponent", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c2n", "[", "n", "]"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", "hbar"}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"n", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "NonNegativeIntegers"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exponent is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 " at every order, even by construction, and, just as important, the sources \
are diagonal only: on stationary paths each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 " folds into the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 " channel (the essay's Part VII), so the local truncation generates no cross \
channel at any order. The conclusion is then itself a one-line theorem on the \
general covariance: feed the Lyapunov solution any even, diagonal source and \
the steady covariance is even in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"par", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"sigmaGen", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dxp", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dxx", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"u", " ", 
          RowBox[{"hbar", "^", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "2"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"dpp", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"v", " ", 
          RowBox[{"hbar", "^", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "2"}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], 
       "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"par", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"par", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "hbar"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Integers"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "identically, for arbitrary weights ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],
 " and every order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 ". An even function cannot contain the odd ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "3", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 " term. What the local expansion cannot produce, the exact theory does: the \
missing object is a cross coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],
 ", which enters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],
 " but not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 ", and the inversion below shows it is precisely what holding the mean-force \
covariance demands."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The momentum entry fails harder. The momentum variance has its own \
Matsubara representation (Grabert-Schramm-Ingold), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"M", "F"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", "2", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "+", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 " with the Drude damping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalOmega]", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], "+", "\[CapitalOmega]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 "; its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],
 " coefficient comes by the same derivative-under-the-sum route as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],
 ", and its large-cutoff expansion:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"p1", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"M", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"D", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Om", "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "Om"}], 
                   ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "gam", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Om", "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "Om"}], 
                   ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
           "gam"}], "]"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gam", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"p1asy", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
     RowBox[{"p1", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Om", ",", " ", "Infinity", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The expansion carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["log",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2", "\[Pi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],
 ": the momentum correction has no cutoff-free limit. Its logarithmic slope \
is exact:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p1asy", ",", " ", "Om"}], "]"}], " ", "Om"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The representation itself deserves the same independent check the position \
variance got: the Matsubara sum at finite ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],
 " against the fluctuation-dissipation integral with the Drude response ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "-", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], " ", "2", 
       StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalOmega]", "/", 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "-", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 ", two genuinely different routes to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubsuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"M", "F"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"M", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kB", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"7", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Om", " ", "=", " ", "50"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"M", " ", "kB", " ", "T", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"NSum", "[", "\n", "       ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", "2", " ", "gam", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Om", "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "Om"}], 
                   ")"}]}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", "2", " ", "gam", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Om", "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"nu", "[", "n", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "Om"}], 
                   ")"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{"NSumTerms", " ", "->", " ", "3000"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", " ", "->", " ", "25"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
         ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"M", "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", "/", "Pi"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"NIntegrate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Coth", "[", 
            RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Im", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1", "/", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"M", " ", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"I", " ", "w", " ", "2", " ", "gam", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Om", "/", 
                   RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{"Om", " ", "-", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"I", " ", "w"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], 
            "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", " ", "->", " ", "20"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", " ", "10"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two routes coincide, so the momentum representation, and with it the \
log and its slope, stands on its own numbers rather than on the citation. The \
true equilibrium momentum variance grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["ln",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2", "\[Pi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],
 ", divergent in exactly the scaling limit the paper takes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],
 " at fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],
 ". The divergence is a classical result, the ultraviolet sensitivity of the \
Ohmic momentum dispersion of Grabert, Weiss and Talkner (Z. Phys. B ",
 StyleBox["55",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 87 (1984)); what is presented here is its form in the paper's own \
ordering of scales. The ordering matters and must be stated: the logarithm, \
and its oddness in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],
 ", belong to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[CapitalOmega]", "\[GreaterGreater]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],
 ", the regime the paper works in. In the opposite ordering ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[CapitalOmega]", "\[LessLess]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],
 " the same sum gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "6", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],
 ", even in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],
 " and linear in the cutoff, which is the form in Hilt, Thomas and Lutz's \
high-temperature appendix. Either way the conclusion for the family is the \
same exclusion: the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],
 " momentum correction is cutoff-dependent in every ordering, so a generator \
whose coefficients are free of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],
 " cannot track it, and matching the ",
 StyleBox["bare Gibbs", "TI"],
 " variance at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 ", which is what the paper's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],
 " achieves, is the only cutoff-free equilibrium statement available. There \
is an irony worth stating: the generator built to penalize high-frequency \
quantum fluctuations necessarily omits the physical high-frequency dressing \
of the momentum, because that dressing is exactly what diverges when the \
cutoff is removed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The correlation entry needs no computation at all. The global Gibbs state \
is invariant under time reversal, which flips ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["P", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],
 " and every bath momentum while fixing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],
 " is odd under it, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"M", "F"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],
 " exactly, at every order in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],
 ". The completely positive steady state cannot comply once ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 " is pinned near the Einstein value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],
 " by classical equipartition, which any candidate thermal generator must \
respect: then complete positivity requires ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "8", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 " (feature A), and the steady correlation is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],
 ", so every such completely positive member carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "8", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],
 ", bounded away from the true value by the positivity floor itself (the \
constraint of Artini and co-workers, read as an equilibrium error bound; the \
paper's point sits at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "6", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],
 ", above the floor by the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "/", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],
 " as in feature A)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The inversion, and what it costs on the Caldeira-Leggett slice.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Ask directly for the constant-coefficient generator whose steady \
covariance is a prescribed equilibrium-grade ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],
 ", diagonal because time reversal forbids a steady correlation. Two \
restrictions define the class being asked about, and both must be said out \
loud. The friction is the ",
 StyleBox["translation-covariant", "TI"],
 ", position-coupled one of the paper's generator, acting on the momentum row \
alone; this is fidelity to the generator as stated, not a microscopic \
necessity (a position-coupled bath at finite cutoff produces \
frequency-dependent friction, which is where the section ends up), and the \
general quadratic Lindbladian has a wider, two-parameter friction (Isar, \
Sandulescu and Scheid, Int. J. Mod. Phys. E ",
 StyleBox["3",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 635 (1994)), revisited below; \"slice\" abbreviates the \
translation-covariant class throughout. And the Hamiltonian is the bare one, \
no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],
 " frequency renormalization, matching the generator as the paper states it. \
Within the slice the Lyapunov map inverts uniquely:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sigT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"aa", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "bb"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"diffusion", "[", 
        RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"lyapInv", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Amat", ",", " ", "sigT"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", "solT"}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One generator per target, holding its second moments stationary (stationary \
moments, not equilibrium in the strong sense: quantum detailed balance is a \
stricter requirement, the one imposed in the general characterization of \
thermal Gaussian semigroups by Toscano and Nicacio, Phys. Rev. A ",
 StyleBox["106",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 062207 (2022), and not tested here). The anatomy is forced: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 " identically, which is what keeps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],
 "; the momentum channel carries the full target variance; the cross \
coefficient carries the anisotropy, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],
 ". This is the Caldeira-Leggett-slice specialization of thermal-generator \
formulas that exist in the literature (Isar-Sandulescu-Scheid give exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"q", "q"}], "TI"]], "\[Proportional]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],
 ", vanishing on this slice, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"p", "q"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],
 " at the Gibbs target), so the inversion itself is not new; what it is being \
used for is. For the bare Gibbs target the cross coefficient vanishes, by the \
isotropy of the Gibbs covariance:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"sPPgibbs", " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"M", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", "sXXgibbs"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],
 " the unique stationary-moment generator is the quantum-corrected \
Caldeira-Leggett equation of section A, cross-free. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],
 " the mean-force target breaks isotropy, and because the inversion's cross \
coefficient is linear in the target, substituting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"G", "i", "b", "b", "s"}], "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"G", "i", "b", "b", "s"}], "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],
 " into it reduces, by the isotropy just shown, to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],
 ": the cutoff dependence and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "3", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 " term land in the one coefficient the local kernel expansion cannot supply. \
The positivity ledger follows in one line from the general covariance's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 ": a diagonal target forces ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],
 ", hence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "-", "4", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],
 ", and the same line holds verbatim under any drift renormalization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "*"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "\[Rule]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "*"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],
 ". The cells spell it out. The slice inversion gives"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
    RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
     RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/.",
    " ", "solT"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", 
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "4"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 ". The quadratic term is ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " an equilibration cost; it is the price of insisting on the bare \
Hamiltonian. Every diagonal covariance above the vacuum floor (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"a", "b"}], "TI"]], ">", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],
 ") is the Gibbs covariance of a unique effective oscillator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "*"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "*"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 " at the same temperature (the mean-force effective Hamiltonian of Hilt, \
Thomas and Lutz; the mean-force literature's own prescription is to \
renormalize the system Hamiltonian, Timofeev and Trushechkin, \
arXiv:2204.00599), and re-running the inversion with the renormalized drift \
removes the quadratic term exactly:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"AmatR", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "Ms"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "Ms"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"ws", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gam"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solR", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"diffusion", "[", 
        RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"lyapInv", "[", 
        RowBox[{"AmatR", ",", " ", "sigT"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
     RowBox[{"kossakowski", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dxx", ",", " ", "dpp", ",", " ", "dxp"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/.",
     " ", "solR"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"bb", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"aa", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Ms", "^", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"ws", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What no renormalization removes: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],
 " exactly, the Caldeira-Leggett value, still strictly negative. On the \
slice, holding ",
 StyleBox["any", "TI"],
 " diagonal covariance exactly stationary costs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],
 ", Hamiltonian renormalization or not. This statement is not new either: the \
floor is the diffusion constraint of Dekker and Valsakumar (Phys. Lett. A ",
 StyleBox["104",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 67 (1984)), and its failure on the slice at ",
 StyleBox["every", "TI"],
 " frequency and mass, which is exactly the \"any target, any renormalization\
\" content, is stated below Eq. (3.26) of Isar's review of the \
thermal-generator formulas (quant-ph/0602149): at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 " the thermal-stationarity constraint reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],
 ". What the cells add is only the packaging as a target-independent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 " ledger. Complete positivity therefore buys its Lindblad form by giving up \
exactness, and the paper's point is the thermal-optimal completely positive \
compromise at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The slice matters, because off it the story inverts. Widen the friction to \
the two-parameter family, drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "{", "{", "-", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "-", 
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "-", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "}", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 ", and evaluate the Dekker-Valsakumar slack of the generator that holds the \
exact Gibbs covariance stationary:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"A2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"lam", " ", "-", " ", "mu"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "M"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "M"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"lam", " ", "+", " ", "mu"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"slack", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lyapInv", "[", 
         RowBox[{"A2", ",", " ", "sigGibbs"}], "]"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Det", "[", "d", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lam", "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", "slack"}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The slack is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "2"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\\", "coth"}], "2"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 ". On the Caldeira-Leggett slice ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 " it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],
 ", negative at every temperature, the statement above. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],
 " it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["csch",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["positive at every temperature", "TI"],
 ": the textbook quantum-optical damped oscillator, completely positive, \
constant coefficients, exact Gibbs stationary state to all orders in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 ". This dichotomy is the published theorem of Artini and co-workers \
(arXiv:2507.23322): every translation-covariant completely positive quadratic \
master equation with a confining potential ends in a non-equilibrium steady \
state, and only breaking translation covariance, by fine-tuning against the \
system Hamiltonian, restores an equilibrium; the cell above is their theorem \
as a single closed form. Two refinements are worth reading off it. The \
tension needs the potential as well as the friction: for a free particle the \
momentum marginal is exactly Maxwellian on the slice (the equilibration \
statement Artini and co-workers make there; the steady correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 " still survives, the limit cell above), which is consistent with the \
essay's Part VII, where the free-particle kernel tower truncates exactly at \
two operators. And the boundary of the completely positive equilibrating \
region is exactly critical, solvable outright:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Reduce", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"slack", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", "mu", ",", " ", 
    "Reals"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The window is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],
 ", and its distance from the Caldeira-Leggett point at high temperature:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lam", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sech", "[", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
         RowBox[{"w0", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "kB", " ", "T"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"T", ",", " ", "Infinity", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The excluded band around ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],
 " has width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "/", "8", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],
 " at high temperature: the obstruction sits on a knife edge, not in a broad \
forbidden zone. The physical price of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 " stays visible: symmetric damping of both quadratures is an energy-basis \
(rotating-wave) coupling, not the position-coupled bath of the microscopic \
model, and it gives up the translation-covariant free-particle limit that the \
Caldeira-Leggett friction keeps."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact dynamics shares the slice's signature. The Hu-Paz-Zhang master \
equation, derived from the same Feynman-Vernon influence functional without \
the locality truncation, carries no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],
 " term and does carry a time-dependent cross-diffusion coefficient (the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],
 " term in Halliwell and Yu, quant-ph/9508004), and its late-time state is \
the mean-force state (Suba\:015f\[DotlessI] and co-workers). The ledger then \
makes one falsifiable prediction about that published object: since the \
asymptotic Hu-Paz-Zhang generator sits on the slice, ends on a diagonal \
covariance, and so must have a vanishing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],
 " coefficient, its asymptotic Kossakowski data must obey ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "-", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Infinity]", "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 ", exact quantum Brownian motion is asymptotically non-completely-positive \
with a quantified deficit. The quantitative identification of the asymptotic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],
 " with the slice inversion's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 " is untested here, and is not even well posed until the frequency \
convention is pinned, since Hu-Paz-Zhang also renormalizes the frequency and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 " shifts linearly under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0", "2"], "\[Rule]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"*", "2"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],
 " at fixed target. Next steps 3 states both checks with the convention fixed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Verdict, and what is new here.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The completely positive steady state's deviations from bare Gibbs are not \
mean-force corrections in disguise (the short answer needed only feature A \
and time reversal). Nearly everything else in this section is the literature, \
assembled: the mean-force state as the true late-time state (Suba\:015f\
\[DotlessI] et al.), its closed-form covariance and high-temperature \
expansion (Grabert-Schramm-Ingold; the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Zeta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "3", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],
 " term is simply that expansion's first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],
 "-dependent order), the momentum-dispersion cutoff sensitivity in both \
orderings (Grabert-Weiss-Talkner; Hilt-Thomas-Lutz), the effective mean-force \
oscillator (Hilt-Thomas-Lutz), the thermal-generator inversion formulas and \
the slice's thermal-stationarity impossibility at every frequency and mass \
(Isar-Sandulescu-Scheid; Isar quant-ph/0602149, Eq. (3.26)), the positivity \
floor (Dekker-Valsakumar), the translation-covariance dichotomy including the \
fine-tuned escape (Artini and co-workers), the general second-order mismatch \
for completely positive steady states (Lee and Yeo, discrete spectra) and \
Redfield's escape through frequency-dependent rates (Thingna-Wang-H\
\[ADoubleDot]nggi). What this section adds is small and specific: the parity \
scoping (no one had asked whether the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],
 " tower's even, diagonal Lyapunov sources can produce the odd-in-",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],
 " mean-force corrections; they cannot), the mean-force target run through \
the slice inversion with the resulting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 " in closed form, the exactly-critical boundary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["sech",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],
 " read off the slack, and the prediction that the asymptotic Hu-Paz-Zhang \
generator is non-completely-positive with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "-", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Infinity]", "2"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],
 ". The practical audience is first of all this document's own feature A, \
which motivates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],
 " by thermalization and thereby invites over-reading: the equilibrium \
content of the paper's generator is the bare Gibbs state at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],
 " for quadratic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 ", and no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],
 " equilibrium physics should be read off it (for anharmonic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],
 " even the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],
 " verdict is open, feature Engine's territory, since the position diffusion \
then sustains entropy production, Artini). In the generator's own validity \
window the missed position correction is doubly small, suppressed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "/", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],
 " together; the momentum entry, cutoff-divergent, is the one with teeth. A \
reader who needs the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 " equilibrium has published routes: the mean-force Hamiltonian \
renormalization (Timofeev-Trushechkin), Redfield-class frequency-dependent \
rates (Thingna-Wang-H\[ADoubleDot]nggi), or the canonically consistent master \
equation of Becker, Schnell and Thingna (Phys. Rev. Lett. ",
 StyleBox["129",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 200403 (2022)), whose steady state is the mean-force state to second \
order and which is, consistently with everything above, not completely \
positive. Two reconciliations keep the documents consistent: the essay's \
convergent tower refines the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 " covariance toward bare Gibbs, exactly the right target at that order, and \
says nothing about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],
 "; and the paper makes no equilibrium claim at all, so nothing here \
contradicts it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],

Cell["C. The Wigner Fokker-Planck picture (set up)", "Section",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "TO DEVELOP. Wigner-transforming the operator equation gives, for quadratic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],
 ", an exact Klein-Kramers / Fokker-Planck equation"
}], "Text",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       FractionBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["M", "TI"]]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"p", "W"}], "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox[
       UnderscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[
           RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]]}], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
       RowBox[{"=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", 
         StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox[
       UnderscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[
           RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]]}], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
       RowBox[{"=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           RowBox[{"6", 
            StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
            SubscriptBox[
             StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
             StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
            StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox[
       UnderscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"2", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[
           RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]]}], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
       RowBox[{"=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0", " ", 
         StyleBox["here",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "written for the general three-coefficient family and specialized by the \
underbraces to the paper's point, where the cross term vanishes (it is the \
very term the mean-force section shows correct equilibration would need). The \
momentum diffusion is the classical Einstein term; the position diffusion, \
from the new ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],
 " term, is of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],
 " and is a purely quantum smoothing in position that erases sub-Planck \
(interference) structure. This is the classicalization of feature B seen in \
phase space, and it makes the classical limit transparent: as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],
 " the position diffusion vanishes and the equation becomes the classical \
Kramers equation. Tasks: derive the transform and pin the coefficients \
symbolically (confirming the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],
 " position diffusion), solve the Gaussian propagator, and hand the \
anharmonic PDE (with its Moyal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]\[Prime]"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],
 " corrections) to the simulation track."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Engine. The moment hierarchy for general ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],
 " (the tool for A, B, and beyond)"
}], "Section",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Features A and B are the harmonic-case shadow of a general structure. The \
adjoint generator gives, for any observable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["O", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]", "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],
 " with"
}], "Text",
 CellID->485911656,ExpressionUUID->"2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]", "\[Dagger]"], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]], ",", 
     StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], "{", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "}", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"P", "P"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"X", "P"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->181917407,ExpressionUUID->"519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "evaluated with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],
 ". This is a Weyl-algebra computation, so the tool is ",
 Cell["/nca-route", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],
 " (encode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],
 " as generators, apply ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]", "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],
 ", reduce to a normal form, cross-check against a Fock-matrix carrier). The \
first two moment layers, for any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1906087345,ExpressionUUID->"3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],

